{% block howtoModal %}
  <div id="howto-epiphone" class="decoder-modal hidden" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="howto-epiphone-title">
    <div class="decoder-modal-backdrop" data-modal-close></div>
    <div class="decoder-modal-content" role="document">
      <button type="button" class="decoder-modal-close" aria-label="Close dialog" data-modal-close>&times;</button>
      <div class="decoder-modal-header">
        <h2 id="howto-epiphone-title">How to decode an Epiphone serial number</h2>
        <p class="decoder-modal-subtitle">A quick manual method when you don't want to use a decoder.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="decoder-modal-body">
        <p>Epiphone serial numbers generally use a FYYMMRRRR format (Factory, Year, Month, Ranking) since 1993, allowing for easy dating.</p>
        <ul class="decoder-howto-steps">
          <li><strong>Letters:</strong> Represent the factory (e.g., S = Samick, U = Unsung, R = Peerless).</li>
          <li><strong>First 2 Numbers (post‑1993):</strong> Year of manufacture (e.g., 02 = 2002).</li>
          <li><strong>Next 2 Numbers:</strong> Month (e.g., 05 = May).</li>
          <li><strong>Remaining Numbers:</strong> Unit production number.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Common Serial Number Formats &amp; Decoding</h3>
        <ul class="decoder-howto-steps">
          <li><strong>Modern (1993–2008):</strong> Example S02021234 → S (Samick, Korea), 02 (2002), 02 (February), 1234 (Production).</li>
          <li><strong>Modern (2008–Present):</strong> Example 15122300123 → 15 (2015), 12 (December), 23 (Factory/format code), 00123 (Production).</li>
          <li><strong>Elite/Elitist Models:</strong> Typically F YY SSSS (F = Factory, Y = Year, S = Sequential).</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Key Factory Letter Codes</h3>
        <ul class="decoder-howto-steps">
          <li><strong>B:</strong> Bohart, Czech Republic</li>
          <li><strong>DW:</strong> DeaWon, China</li>
          <li><strong>F:</strong> Fuji-gen, Japan</li>
          <li><strong>I:</strong> Saein, Korea</li>
          <li><strong>J:</strong> Pallet, China</li>
          <li><strong>K:</strong> Korea Insung</li>
          <li><strong>MC:</strong> Muse, China</li>
          <li><strong>R:</strong> Peerless, Korea</li>
          <li><strong>S:</strong> Samick, Korea</li>
          <li><strong>SI:</strong> Samick, Indonesia</li>
          <li><strong>T:</strong> Terada, Japan</li>
          <li><strong>U:</strong> Unsung, Korea</li>
          <li><strong>EE:</strong> Qingdao, China</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Other Scenarios</h3>
        <ul class="decoder-howto-steps">
          <li><strong>Pre‑1994:</strong> Often 7–8 digits without a factory letter, or sometimes missing entirely.</li>
          <li><strong>Japanese Models:</strong> Often use different, sometimes stamped, formats.</li>
          <li><strong>No Serial:</strong> Some very old Epiphones or refinished models may lack a visible number.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="decoder-modal-gallery">
          <figure>
